{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And there was no water for the congregation.</b> When Miriam died the well departed, for the well was in the merit of Miriam — she had the merit of water derived from Moses, as it says (Exodus 2:4): ״ותתצב אחותו מרחוק״. And the fact that it departed now, upon her death, is proof that it was with them in her merit; and from here it follows that throughout all forty years the well was with them." "<b>And they say</b> in the Midrash (Numbers 21:17), ״אז ישיר ישראל את השירה הזאת״ — this song was said at the end of forty years, while the well was given to them at the beginning of the forty."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:07.054294130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}